WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:02.890
This imaging system is designed

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:06.020
to have vision that works like our eyes do

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:08.720
These little lenses are used
to create images

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:12.980
with higher resolution in
the center than at the edges

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:14.720
Our eyes work the same way

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.100
thanks to a region
called the fovea,

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:20.200
which is rich in light receptors

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:23.060
Foveated electronic sensors can see a wide,

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:26.700
low-resolution view and
a narrower, high-resolution view

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:30.240
at the same time, instead
of one or the other

00:00:30.249 --> 00:00:31.069
Which means

00:00:31.069 --> 00:00:32.749
that this camera can capture a scene

00:00:32.749 --> 00:00:37.729
at low and high resolution simultaneously

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:40.410
Having a wide view with
high resolution in the center

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:42.289
preserves detail where it’s needed

00:00:42.289 --> 00:00:45.559
without sacrificing processing time

00:00:45.559 --> 00:00:48.299
In the camera, a set of
four compound lenses

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:53.400
is 3D printed directly onto
an image sensing chip

00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:55.950
Some of these lenses see from a wide angle,

00:00:55.950 --> 00:01:00.480
while others take a narrower
view with higher resolution

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:03.460
The information from each
lens is digitally combined

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:05.380
to create a foveated image

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:08.640
with the most information
in the center

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:10.780
A foveated camera can do things like

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:12.600
helping self-driving cars make

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:16.320
quick judgments based
on visual information

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:19.180
At 300 square microns in size with lenses

00:01:19.190 --> 00:01:21.470
only a few tens of microns across,

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:25.560
this camera is unique in its small
size and image quality

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:28.220
There’s still room to improve
the manufacturing time

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:30.880
and optical performance of this device

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:32.690
But it could be a boon to engineers

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:36.130
who need a device with
quick, sharp eagle eyes

